  "details": "I'm a primarily VR user, who uses Holoport (third-person comfort locomotion) mode. However, I kept finding that my Holoport setting was being disabled at random, on launch.  I finally figured out how to reproduce it: it's disabled any time you launch Desktop mode (and REMAINS disabled even after returning to VR!)\nTo fully spell it out:\n1. Launch in VR mode, and enable holoport if it's not already on.\n2. Relaunch, again in VR mode, and note that holoport remains enabled as it should -- touching the joystick moves your character in third-person.\n3. Relaunch, this time in DESKTOP mode.\n4. Relaunch back into VR again, and NOW, touching the joystick will move your whole viewpoint around, dizzyingly!\n5. Go into the settings and re-enable Holoport.\n6. Relaunch in VR mode again, and Holoport remains enabled; only Desktop launches overwrite the setting.",
